{"id": "EUVD-2026-81747", "enisaUuid": "085786ee-792d-3f87-a6c2-967a1c0e23ca", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: scope session state changes to bound connections\n\nksmbd_all_conn_set_status() treats every connection whose transient\nbinding flag is set as belonging to the target SessionId.  A logoff or\nsession replacement can consequently move an unrelated connection to\nNEED_RECONNECT or NEED_SETUP.\n\nPass the target session itself and select connections using either the\nconnection-local session xarray or the session's permanent channel list.\nUse the same association test while waiting for requests to drain.\n\nSerialize session-wide status changes under request_lock and do not\noverwrite EXITING or RELEASING. Protect the shutdown transition with the\nsame lock so a concurrent session update cannot revive a closing\nconnection.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:06:47", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:50:09", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3deefd5fb1368e2577144b0961b1a5df26b587d1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3d66f3ec3c69fa242939a9f9e6815df33390b1bb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1ff0e41afbe73240a7d7b96d4e8e86d0aaf0fe0b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0875872718b98e8530fbc634e5aa7dbd3253b80d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c50e628122aed077695669e25b842e778511a43d"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90154", "GHSA-c8qh-mfc7-v6c7"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "05a549e4-41d8-39e2-9fe1-223a8540412b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15"}, {"id": "07eb1758-54c9-3bb3-9049-4b212e6eb995", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f5a544e3bab78142207e0242d22442db85ba1eff <3deefd5fb1368e2577144b0961b1a5df26b587d1"}, {"id": "29840d4c-d1ee-3a10-9e5f-c3908822615f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id":